### Mockito Matrices

Mockito provides a `@.mockito.Parameters` annotation that allows you to specify multiple parameters for a mock object. This allows you to assign different values to multiple fields.

```java
@Mock
private PasswordRepository passwordRepository;

@.magic
private int passwordId;

testPasswordRepository(
    passwordRepository,
    passwordMapper,
    passwordRepository,
    passwordMapper,
    passwordRepository,
    passwordMapper
) {
    // Set passwordId to 100
    when(passwordRepository.findByPasswordId(passwordId)).thenReturn(PasswordObject.class);

    verify(passwordRepository, times(1)).findByPasswordId(passwordId);

    // Check passwordId can be assigned multiple times
    assertNotNull(passwordId);
    assertNotSame(passwordId, 0);
}
```

### Mockito Context

Mockito's `@Mock` annotation is used to create a mock object without any additional configuration. When used with `@FalseMock` (means NOT-METHODSSever terminated) [x] x Titanic mocking is also canceled and a real promise should be made.

```java
@FalseMock
private PasswordRepository passwordRepository;

testPasswordRepository(
    passwordRepository,
    passwordRepository,
    passwordRepository
) {
    // Test GetPassword method
    when(passwordRepositoryindrome(getPasswordId())).thenReturn(PasswordObject.class);

    assertNotNull(passwordRepository);
}
```

